---
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>CostMate — Know your real product costs</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="CostMate calculates the true unit cost of every product you make — materials, machines, energy, and overhead included. Stop guessing your prices. Coming soon to Google Play and the App Store."
    />
    <meta property="og:title" content="CostMate — Know your real product costs" />
    <meta
      property="og:description"
      content="Product costing for small manufacturers, workshops, and food producers. Materials, machines, energy, and overhead — all in one true unit cost."
    />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://obura.io/costmate" />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://obura.io/store-assets/feature-graphic.png" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <nav class="topnav">
      <a class="brand" href="/">obura<span>.studios</span></a>
      <a class="nav-cta" href="#pricing">Pricing</a>
    </nav>

    <!-- 1. Hero -->
    <header class="hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="kicker">By Obura Studios</p>
        <div class="app-title">
          <span class="app-mark">
            <img src="/store-assets/icon-512.png" alt="" width="512" height="512" />
          </span>
          <h1>CostMate</h1>
        </div>
        <p class="value-prop">
          Stop guessing your prices.<br />Know what your products
          <em>really</em> cost.
        </p>
        <p class="flow-line">Materials · Equipment · Overhead · Real margins</p>
        <p class="sub">
          CostMate calculates the true unit cost of every product you make —
          materials, machines, energy, and overhead included. Built for small
          manufacturers, workshops, and food producers. No accounting degree
          required.
        </p>
        <div class="store-row">
          <span class="coming-badge">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 6v6l4 2" /><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" /></svg>
            Coming soon to Google Play &amp; the App Store
          </span>
        </div>
        <p class="langs">Available in English, Turkish, French, and German.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-visual">
        <div class="phone">
          <img
            src="/store-assets/shot-05-cost-breakdown.png"
            alt="CostMate cost breakdown screen showing materials, overhead, total cost, and profit per unit"
            width="1440"
            height="2880"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main>
      <!-- 2. The problem -->
      <section class="problem" aria-label="The problem">
        <h2 class="visually-hidden">The problem</h2>
        <div class="problem-grid">
          <div class="pain">
            <h3>Guessed prices</h3>
            <p>
              "It feels like about €8" is not a price. If your cost is really
              €8.40, every sale loses money — and you won't see it for months.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="pain">
            <h3>Forgotten hidden costs</h3>
            <p>
              The oven's electricity. The machine you paid €3,000 for. The
              rent. They belong in every unit you make — most makers leave
              them out.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="pain">
            <h3>Spreadsheet chaos</h3>
            <p>
              One broken formula, three outdated tabs, and no idea which
              version is current. Spreadsheets weren't built for recipes and
              machine hours.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 3. Features -->
      <section class="features" id="features">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>Everything that goes into one unit — counted</h2>
          <p>Real features, no filler. This is what CostMate does.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-group">
          <h3 class="group-title">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7h16M4 12h16M4 17h10" /></svg>
            Core costing engine
          </h3>
          <div class="feature-grid">
            <article class="feature">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="3" width="7" height="7" rx="1.5" /><rect x="14" y="3" width="7" height="7" rx="1.5" /><rect x="8.5" y="14" width="7" height="7" rx="1.5" /><path d="M6.5 10v2h11v-2M12 12v2" /></svg>
              <h4>Recipe-based costs</h4>
              <p>
                Build products from materials — or from other products.
                Multi-level recipes handle real production, and batch logic
                knows how much one batch yields and how long it takes.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v18M5 8h7M5 16h14" /><circle cx="17" cy="8" r="2.5" /><circle cx="9" cy="16" r="2.5" /></svg>
              <h4>True cost breakdown</h4>
              <p>
                Every unit cost is split into materials + equipment +
                overhead, shown separately. You see exactly where the money
                goes.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 19c3-1 4-3 4-6l8-8 3 3-8 8c-3 0-5 1-7 3z" /><path d="M14 7l3 3" /></svg>
              <h4>Waste priced in</h4>
              <p>
                Set waste per ingredient as a percentage or a fixed amount.
                Scrap, trim, and spillage stop being invisible losses.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 4v6a5 5 0 0 0 10 0V4" /><path d="M5 4h14M9 20h6M12 15v5" /></svg>
              <h4>Unit conversions</h4>
              <p>
                Weight, volume (with density), and piece-based materials all
                work together. Buy in liters, use in grams — CostMate does
                the math.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-group">
          <h3 class="group-title">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13 2 4 14h6l-1 8 9-12h-6z" /></svg>
            The costs most tools ignore
          </h3>
          <div class="feature-grid">
            <article class="feature">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3" /><path d="M12 5V3M12 21v-2M5 12H3M21 12h-2M6.3 6.3 4.9 4.9M19.1 19.1l-1.4-1.4M6.3 17.7l-1.4 1.4M19.1 4.9l-1.7 1.4" /></svg>
              <h4>Machine cost per minute</h4>
              <p>
                Purchase price, depreciation over useful life, salvage value,
                maintenance, and energy use in kW — turned into an hourly
                machine cost and applied to each product by minutes of use.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21c-4 0-6.5-2.6-6.5-6C5.5 10 12 3 12 3s6.5 7 6.5 12c0 3.4-2.5 6-6.5 6z" /></svg>
              <h4>Four energy types</h4>
              <p>
                Electricity, gas, coal, and wood — each machine uses the
                right one, at the right price.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 21h18M5 21V8l7-5 7 5v13" /><path d="M9 21v-6h6v6" /></svg>
              <h4>Overhead, spread fairly</h4>
              <p>
                Rent, salaries, insurance — spread over your monthly
                production hours and baked into every unit cost
                automatically.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-group">
          <h3 class="group-title">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" /><path d="M12 7v5l3 3" /></svg>
            Price history done right
          </h3>
          <div class="feature-grid two">
            <article class="feature">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="16" rx="2" /><path d="M3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4" /></svg>
              <h4>Prices with effective dates</h4>
              <p>
                Material and energy prices are stored with the date they took
                effect. Update a price today without rewriting yesterday.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 19V5M4 19h16" /><path d="M7 15l4-4 3 2 6-6" /></svg>
              <h4>Historical reports stay true</h4>
              <p>
                Past production is costed with the prices of that day. Your
                March report still shows March's real costs — even after
                energy prices jump in April.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-group">
          <h3 class="group-title">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v18M8 7c0-1.5 1.5-2.5 4-2.5s4 1 4 2.5-1.5 2.3-4 3-4 1.5-4 3 1.5 2.5 4 2.5 4-1 4-2.5" /></svg>
            Profitability at a glance
          </h3>
          <div class="feature-grid two">
            <article class="feature">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20.5 12A8.5 8.5 0 1 1 12 3.5" /><path d="M12 12V3.5A8.5 8.5 0 0 1 20.5 12z" /></svg>
              <h4>Profit and margin per product</h4>
              <p>
                Enter your sale price and instantly see profit and margin for
                every product. No formulas, no exports.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2" /><path d="M7 15v-3M12 15V9M17 15v-5" /></svg>
              <h4>Best &amp; worst sellers dashboard</h4>
              <p>
                A dashboard highlights your most and least profitable
                products, so you know what to push and what to reprice.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-group">
          <h3 class="group-title">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 3v4M3 5h4M19 13v4M17 15h4M11 5l2.5 5.5L19 13l-5.5 2.5L11 21l-2.5-5.5L3 13l5.5-2.5z" /></svg>
            Easy start
          </h3>
          <div class="feature-grid two">
            <article class="feature">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6h16M4 6l2 13h12l2-13" /><path d="M9 11h6" /></svg>
              <h4>Guided setup wizard</h4>
              <p>
                Business name and logo, currency, energy prices — with
                one-tap typical prices for your country — and your monthly
                production hours. Step by step, a few minutes total.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="3" width="8" height="8" rx="1.5" /><rect x="13" y="3" width="8" height="8" rx="1.5" /><rect x="3" y="13" width="8" height="8" rx="1.5" /><rect x="13" y="13" width="8" height="8" rx="1.5" /></svg>
              <h4>Explore with sample data</h4>
              <p>
                Load a complete demo business — an Italian restaurant, a lamp
                workshop, a coffee shop &amp; bakery, or an electronics
                startup — and poke around before entering your own data.
                Removable at any time.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-group">
          <h3 class="group-title">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21s-7-4.5-9-9a5.2 5.2 0 0 1 9-4.8A5.2 5.2 0 0 1 21 12c-2 4.5-9 9-9 9z" /></svg>
            Everyday comfort
          </h3>
          <div class="feature-grid">
            <article class="feature">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="2" /><circle cx="9" cy="11" r="2" /><path d="M3 17l5-4 3 2 4-4 6 5" /></svg>
              <h4>Photos, icons &amp; notes</h4>
              <p>
                Give every material and product a photo or icon. Add notes
                with clickable links to suppliers or datasheets.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3a9 9 0 1 0 9 9 7 7 0 0 1-9-9z" /></svg>
              <h4>Light &amp; dark theme</h4>
              <p>
                Comfortable in the workshop at noon and at the desk at
                midnight. Sign in with Google or email.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l7 3v5c0 5-3 8-7 10-4-2-7-5-7-10V6z" /><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4" /></svg>
              <h4>Privacy-friendly</h4>
              <p>
                No ads. No advertising or analytics SDKs. Your data is never
                sold, and you can delete your account and all data in-app at
                any time.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 4. How it works -->
      <section class="how" id="how-it-works">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>How it works</h2>
          <p>From download to your first real cost in one sitting.</p>
        </div>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>
            <span class="step-num">1</span>
            <h3>Set up your workshop</h3>
            <p>
              The wizard walks you through currency, energy prices, and
              monthly production hours. Add your machines and overhead
              expenses once.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="step-num">2</span>
            <h3>Add materials &amp; recipes</h3>
            <p>
              Enter your materials with prices and waste, then build recipes
              — including batch size and production time.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="step-num">3</span>
            <h3>See your real cost and margin</h3>
            <p>
              CostMate shows the true unit cost of every product and the
              margin at your sale price. Reprice with confidence.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <!-- Screenshots -->
      <section class="shots" aria-label="App screenshots">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>See it in action</h2>
          <p>Real screens from CostMate.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="shots-row">
          <figure>
            <img loading="lazy" src="/store-assets/shot-01-dashboard-welcome.png" alt="Overview screen explaining how materials and equipment come together into products" width="1440" height="2880" />
            <figcaption>Overview &amp; how it works</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img loading="lazy" src="/store-assets/shot-02-dashboard-profit.png" alt="Dashboard listing most and least profitable products" width="1440" height="2880" />
            <figcaption>Most &amp; least profitable</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img loading="lazy" src="/store-assets/shot-03-products.png" alt="Products list with margin per product" width="1440" height="2880" />
            <figcaption>Products with live margins</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img loading="lazy" src="/store-assets/shot-04-recipe.png" alt="Recipe editor with ingredients, waste percentages, and batch total" width="1440" height="2880" />
            <figcaption>Recipes with waste priced in</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img loading="lazy" src="/store-assets/shot-06-whatif.png" alt="What-if planner showing revenue, total profit, and materials needed for a production run" width="1440" height="2880" />
            <figcaption>What-if planning</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img loading="lazy" src="/store-assets/shot-08-equipment.png" alt="Equipment and expenses screen with hourly overhead rate and machine costs" width="1440" height="2880" />
            <figcaption>Machines &amp; overhead rate</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 5. Pricing -->
      <section class="pricing" id="pricing">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>Free to start. Pro when you grow.</h2>
          <p>
            The full costing engine is free. Pro adds room and automation for
            growing businesses.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col"><span class="visually-hidden">Feature</span></th>
                <th scope="col">Free</th>
                <th scope="col" class="pro-col">Pro</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Full costing engine — recipes, machines, energy, overhead</th>
                <td><span class="check" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td>
                <td class="pro-col"><span class="check" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Businesses</th>
                <td>1</td>
                <td class="pro-col">Multiple, with quick switching</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Materials</th>
                <td>Up to 60</td>
                <td class="pro-col">Higher limits</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Products</th>
                <td>Up to 30</td>
                <td class="pro-col">Higher limits</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">
                  Automatic energy-price updates — local electricity and gas
                  reference prices for your country, applied daily
                </th>
                <td><span class="dash" aria-label="Not included">—</span></td>
                <td class="pro-col"><span class="check" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="pricing-note">
          Pro is an auto-renewing subscription via Google Play / App Store.
          Cancel anytime.
        </p>
        <div class="store-row center">
          <span class="coming-badge">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 6v6l4 2" /><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" /></svg>
            Coming soon — prices will be shown in the app
          </span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 6. FAQ -->
      <section class="faq" id="faq">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>Questions, answered</h2>
        </div>
        <details>
          <summary>Is my data safe?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. CostMate has no ads and no advertising or analytics SDKs,
            and your data is never sold. You can delete your account and all
            of your data from inside the app at any time.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Which languages does CostMate support?</summary>
          <p>English, Turkish, French, and German.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I cancel Pro anytime?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. Pro is a standard auto-renewing subscription managed through
            Google Play or the App Store. Cancel there anytime and you keep
            Pro until the end of the paid period.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I try it before entering my own data?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. Load a complete sample business — an Italian restaurant, a
            lamp workshop, a coffee shop &amp; bakery, or an electronics
            startup — and explore every screen with realistic data. Remove it
            with one tap whenever you're ready to start fresh.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How is this different from a spreadsheet?</summary>
          <p>
            A spreadsheet only knows what you type into it. CostMate knows
            how costing works: it depreciates your machines, converts kW into
            cost per minute, spreads your rent over production hours, prices
            in waste, and keeps price history with effective dates so old
            reports stay accurate. No formulas to build, no formulas to
            break.
          </p>
        </details>
      </section>

      <!-- Closing CTA -->
      <section class="closing">
        <h2>Know your numbers before you set your prices.</h2>
        <div class="store-row center">
          <span class="coming-badge big">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 6v6l4 2" /><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" /></svg>
            CostMate is coming soon to Google Play &amp; the App Store
          </span>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <!-- 7. Footer -->
    <footer>
      <p>&copy; {year} Obura</p>
      <nav aria-label="Legal">
        <a href="/costmate/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>
        <a href="/costmate/terms/">Terms of Service</a>
        <a href="/costmate/delete-account/">Account Deletion</a>
      </nav>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #fbfaf8;
    --surface: #ffffff;
    --border: #e8e4dd;
    --text: #1c1b18;
    --muted: #6d685f;
    --accent: #5157e6;
    --accent-strong: #4348d4;
    --accent-soft: #eef0fd;
    --profit: #0f9f6e;
    --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(28, 27, 24, 0.05), 0 8px 24px rgba(28, 27, 24, 0.06);
  }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --bg: #111115;
      --surface: #1a1a20;
      --border: #2a2a32;
      --text: #ecebe8;
      --muted: #98948c;
      --accent: #8b93f8;
      --accent-strong: #a3aafa;
      --accent-soft: #24264a;
      --profit: #34d399;
      --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4), 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
    }
    html {
      color-scheme: dark;
    }
  }

  * {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    margin: 0;
  }

  html {
    color-scheme: light;
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
  }

  body {
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    font-family:
      system-ui,
      -apple-system,
      'Segoe UI',
      sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .visually-hidden {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0 0 0 0);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  svg {
    fill: none;
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 1.7;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  /* Top nav */
  .topnav {
    max-width: 68rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }

  .brand {
    color: var(--text);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .brand span {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .nav-cta {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* Hero */
  .hero {
    max-width: 68rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 1.5rem 4rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 820px) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 0.85fr;
      padding-top: 4.5rem;
    }
  }

  .kicker {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .app-title {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .app-mark {
    display: inline-flex;
    width: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 4rem);
    height: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 4rem);
    border-radius: 26%;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .app-mark img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    display: block;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 800;
